      array("is_admin" => 0,"type" => "teacher", 'profile_updated_date' => null, 'email' => '', 'id' => '21', 'name' => 'Firmino Oliveira da Silva', 'ciencia_vitae' => 'C21A-91DC-B90B', 'orcid' => '', 'id_google_scholar' => '', 'id_researcher' => '', 'id_scopus_author' => '', 'resume' => 'Adjunct professor at ISLA - IPGT (Polytechnic Institute of Management and Technology in Vila Nova de Gaia) with over 20 years teaching at Polytechnic of Porto schools (ISCAP - Accounting and Business School and ESMAD - Media, Arts and Design School) .  He is currently the Director of the Research Center at ISLA-IPGT, the Director of the Master\'s course in Engineering of Technologies and Web Systems, Director of the Degree in Informatics for Electronic Commerce, and he is also the director of the Postgraduate Program in Business Analytics and Data Science. He has over 35 years of professional experience working in companies where he has led numerous IT projects and departments (Telecom (Telecommunications), Credifin/Cetelem (Finance), Autosueco/NORS (Automotive), IBM (Technology) and BPI (Banking)).  In parallel, he regularly provides professional IT training services at major companies where he promotes and teaches professional training courses in the areas of: Business Analytics (supported by Power BI - DAX/M); Data modelling; e-Commerce, Project Management and Advanced Excel Spread Sheet.  He has a degree in Computer Engineering from ISEP - Engineering School of Porto and a master\'s degree in Information Management from FEUP - Faculty of Engineering of Porto. He holds a PhD in Computer Science, with a specialization in Service-Oriented Computing and Service Analytics from TU/e - Eindhoven University of Technology (The Netherlands). His main research interests are: Business Analytics and Data Science, Project Management (Waterfall and Agile methodologies), Enterprise Resource Planning systems, Data Modelling, Blockchain, Service-Oriented Computing, e-Commerce, Industry 4.0 and D